# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.orig
*.rej
*~

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 20. Internal reports leaked at root (mis-quoted PowerShell Write-Host
#     interpreting backslash escapes in C:\aphrody-backup\* paths).
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
/aphrody-backup*
/C:*
/rename-report.json
/rename-dryrun.json
/rename-apply.json
/manifest-scan.json
/tree-scan.json

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 21. Removed sub-projects (block accidental re-introduction)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# crates/{coreutils,util-linux} — were git submodules excluded from workspace,
# removed in the Rust-only pivot. Re-clone on demand if ever needed.
crates/coreutils/
crates/util-linux/

# Pre-commit / Husky / Lefthook config — no auto hooks.
.pre-commit-config.yaml
.husky/
.lefthook.yml
lefthook.yml

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 22. Cross-Claude noise sink
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Peer Claude session in winclean has dropped Steam-monitor screenshots into
# aphrody root twice this session. Off-scope here; canonical location is
# C:/winclean/var/steam-monitor-snapshot*.png. Block at root.
/steam.png
/steam*.png

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 23. mrx scan artifacts (written into cwd by default)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# `mrx scan` and `mrx check` write path.json + monorepo-map.json into the
# scanned root by default. They are reproducible outputs of the binary, not
# checked-in artefacts. CI exports them as job outputs; locally they should
# never be committed.
/path.json
/monorepo-map.json
/map.json

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 24. Claude Code plugin local settings (.claude/aphrody.local.md pattern)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The `aphrody` plugin reads per-project settings from
# `.claude/aphrody.local.md` (cf. plugin-settings standard from plugin-dev).
# These files contain user-local plugin config and must never be committed.
.claude/*.local.md
.claude/*.local.json


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 25. Structural non-trackables (stabilise checkpoint 2026-05-22)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Registered git worktrees (e.g. parallel-agent sandboxes) — never commit.
.claude/worktrees/
# Built tool binaries (n2b etc.) — reproducible, not source.
/bin/
# Stray scratch outputs.
/=ro
/test_localsystem.txt
/webview2_analysis_results.jsonl
/webview2_visualization.html

# ── Réunification 2026-05-27 : sous-arbres py/ go/ ts/ ─────────────────────────
# Les patterns Rust-root ci-dessus (bun.lock, bunfig.toml, tsconfig.json,
# secrets/, …) ne doivent PAS fuir dans les sous-arbres rapatriés : leur propre
# .gitignore imbriqué gouverne leurs vrais artefacts (.venv, node_modules,
# target, results_lora…). On ré-inclut ici leurs fichiers de config/lock suivis.
!go/gogcli/internal/secrets/
!go/**/pnpm-lock.yaml
!go/gogcli/.lefthook.yml
!ts/bun.lock
!ts/bunfig.toml
!ts/**/tsconfig.json
!ts/**/tsconfig.*.json

# --- Merged TS workspace: track build configs the publish CI needs ----------
# The patterns above (tsconfig.json, tsconfig.*.json, turbo.json, bun.lock) were
# inherited from aphrody's Rust-only era. The 2026-06 merge brought in the
# @aphrody-code/* TS packages whose hand-written build configs + the workspace
# lockfile MUST be tracked, or `release-m3-packages.yml`
# (bun install --frozen-lockfile + turbo run build) cannot run. Re-include them:
!/turbo.json
!/bun.lock
!/packages/*/tsconfig.json
!/packages/*/tsconfig.*.json
!/packages/*/turbo.json
